# AGENT SCRATCH/DEBUG FILES (Claude Code & Antigravity), repo-root only.
# Primary control is CLAUDE.md / ANTIGRAVITY.md: throwaway scripts, repro
# cases, and generated test artifacts belong in each model's dedicated
# /tmp working directory, never in the repo tree. This is just the
# backstop in case one slips through anyway -- patterns match the file
# names that have recurred across past cleanups (see #1091).
/scratch*.py
/fix*.py
/patch*.py
/add_*.py
/append_*.py
/generate_*.py
/redos_scanner.py
/remove_invalid_tests.py
/resolve.py
/run_tests.sh
/test_*.py
/update*.py
/wait_test.py
/Makefile.test*
/pr_*body*.md
/pr_*body*.txt
/pr_body.*
/*_lessons.txt
/LESSONS_LEARNED.md
/rewrite_docs.py

# GITGALAXY HEAVY DATA
data/
museum/
museum_2/
*.json
# ...except committed regression-check baselines, e.g. dead_key_audit_baseline.json
# and mypy_audit_baseline.json -- these are source, not generated output.
!tests/*_baseline.json
!tests/*_baseline_*.json
# ...and the shared Claude Code project config (team-wide permissions/hooks/model
# settings). settings.local.json stays ignored -- that one's per-machine/personal.
!.claude/settings.json
# ...and the tri-comparison discrepancy ledger: regenerated by tests/tools/tri_comparison_chart.py,
# but merge_and_save() preserves every human-investigated verdict across runs (see
# tri_comparison_ledger.py's own docstring) -- committed and hand-edited like the baselines
# above, not disposable scan output.
!docs/self_scan/tri_comparison_ledger.json
# ...and its call/import twin (#3641, docs/self_scan/graph_comparison_README.md): same module,
# same hand-edited verdicts, merged by `call_graph_accuracy.py --ledger`.
!docs/self_scan/graph_comparison_ledger.json
# ...and the manual-verification record for zero-comparison-tool languages (no tree-sitter,
# no ctags -- e.g. abap): hand-reviewed and committed like the ledger above, read by
# tests/tools/tri_comparison_chart.py but never written by it.
!docs/self_scan/manual_verification.json
# docs/research: data that backs a research write-up (the Devin port inventory)
!docs/research/*.json
# #4047: the committed mutation scores of the proven ports (tests/tools/mutation_scores.py)
!docs/language_status/mutation_scores.json
# #4270: the measured census use / crucible cases the CICS spec status page renders (cics_spec_status.py)
!docs/language_status/cics_spec_status.json
# #4601: the purchaser-facing evidence reports (burned estates only)
!docs/language_status/evidence_report/*/report.json
# #3315: hand-labelled thin-wrapper verdicts -- source data the wrapper probe scores against.
!tests/tools/wrapper_labels.json
!tests/tools/wrapper_labels_memory_alloc.json
# ...and the COBOL modernization answer key (#3210): hand-verified per-program truth,
# committed and reviewed like the ledger above. A new key file dropped silently by
# the *.json rule above is how its first PR shipped without its own data.
!tests/cobol_mainframe/answer_key/*.json
# ...and the port-invariance pairs' manifest (tests/tools/port_invariance.py): which COBOL file
# each committed det port pairs with.
!tests/cobol_mainframe/port_invariance/pairs.json
# ...and the mixed CJK EBCDIC code-page tables (#3816 part 3a): package data the decoder
# loads at run time, generated once from the JDK by tests/tools/gen_ebcdic_dbcs.py.
!gitgalaxy/core/ebcdic_dbcs/*.json
# ...and the archetype brains + their validation record (#4100): package data the
# classifier loads at run time; archetype-validation.yml refreshes the record on main.
!gitgalaxy/standards/archetype_brains/*.json
# ...and the pinned mainframe corpus manifest (#3213) and the refraction tools'
# ReDoS baseline (#3214): committed source, same reason.
!tests/cobol_mainframe/corpora.json
!tests/cobol_mainframe/tool_regex_redos_baseline.json
!tests/estate_crucible/baseline.json
# ...and the pinned import-graph accuracy corpus manifest (tests/tools/import_graph_accuracy.py).
!tests/import_graph_corpus.json
# ...and the refraction differential's unexplained-delta baseline (#3211).
!tests/cobol_mainframe/refraction_differential_baseline.json
# ...and the mainframe ground-truth ledger (tests/tools/ground_truth_ledger.py).
!tests/cobol_mainframe/ground_truth_ledger.json
# ...and the fresh-estate trial ledger (#3805, tests/tools/trial.py).
!tests/cobol_mainframe/trials.json
# ...and the CICS crucible runner's ratchet ledger and its fixture case (#3989): the fixture is in the
# crucible's format, so its case.json and expected logs are source like the answer keys above.
!tests/cics_crucible/baseline.json
# #4023: the crucible's COBOL coverage ledger (a ratchet, like baseline.json)
!tests/cics_crucible/coverage.json
# ...and the equivalence cases (#3624) and their ports' provenance (#4023 follow-up): source, not output
!tests/equivalence/*/case.json
!tests/equivalence/*/port/provenance.json
# ...and the estates' compile / runtime options (#4704): one file per corpus, source not output
!tests/equivalence/estate_options/*.json
!tests/cics_crucible/ports/*/*/provenance.json
# #4048: the evidence record of each ported program (tests/tools/evidence.py) is source, not output
!tests/equivalence/*/evidence.json
!tests/equivalence/facade_baseline.json
!tests/equivalence/det_sweep_baseline.json
!tests/equivalence/det_sweep_coverage/*.json
!tests/equivalence/infeasible_outcomes.json
!tests/cics_crucible/ports/*/*/evidence.json
!tests/cics_crucible/fixture/**/*.json
*_llm.md
venvs/

